WEBVTT

00:00.924 --> 00:03.718
Josuke, I'm going hunting.

00:04.010 --> 00:05.219
Huh?

00:05.595 --> 00:06.637
And I want you to come along.

00:08.598 --> 00:09.307
Huh?

00:09.391 --> 00:13.891
Hang on, slow down.
Did you say "hunting"?

00:14.604 --> 00:16.230
You don't mean…

00:17.732 --> 00:21.068
we're goin' huntin' for
hotties with nice bodies?

00:21.194 --> 00:23.237
I'm more the romantic type,

00:23.321 --> 00:25.448
so you'll have to show
this newbie the ropes.

00:25.615 --> 00:27.283
I don't know
if I can pull it off…

00:28.159 --> 00:30.578
Akira Otoishi came clean
about his past yesterday.

00:31.079 --> 00:32.080
He did?!

00:32.455 --> 00:36.709
Seems there was a lot we didn't
know about his bow and arrow use.

00:37.085 --> 00:39.337
Turns out he also
shot a rat with the arrow.

00:39.421 --> 00:40.463
A rat?!

00:41.298 --> 00:44.175
But the rat didn't die.

00:44.593 --> 00:47.971
Writhing in agony, it managed
to free itself from the arrow

00:48.096 --> 00:49.222
and headed for the hills.

00:51.600 --> 00:54.227
In other words, it may be a rat,

00:54.311 --> 00:56.730
but it undoubtedly
acquired Stand abilities.

00:57.522 --> 00:59.482
What it can do, I have no idea.

00:59.733 --> 01:02.360
We have to hunt it down
before it can cause any harm.

01:22.589 --> 01:23.214
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

01:23.298 --> 01:25.383
<i>A demon's crept into
our everyday life</i>

01:25.467 --> 01:27.760
<i>It's about to take away
something precious</i>

01:27.844 --> 01:31.097
<i>Our peace has already
crumbled long ago</i>

01:31.848 --> 01:33.933
<i>So casually, so nonchalantly</i>

01:34.017 --> 01:36.352
<i>It's taken from us
before we know it</i>

01:36.436 --> 01:39.689
<i>If we want it back,
now's the chance</i>

01:39.898 --> 01:43.401
<i>With the sharpness of
the piercing arrow</i>

01:44.194 --> 01:47.572
<i>The beauty of two souls united</i>

01:47.656 --> 01:50.241
<i>Wherever you go, chase you</i>

01:50.325 --> 01:52.452
<i>Whenever, chase you</i>

01:52.535 --> 01:54.537
<i>I will chase you</i>

01:54.621 --> 01:56.247
<i>Nowhere to escape</i>

01:56.331 --> 01:58.875
<i>Start running, I will chase you</i>

01:58.958 --> 02:00.960
<i>Tomorrow, chase you</i>

02:01.044 --> 02:03.755
<i>My fists will be the one
to show you</i>

02:03.963 --> 02:08.463
<i>Tenacity decides
who will win or lose</i>

02:09.678 --> 02:14.178
<i>So I chase you</i>

02:17.519 --> 02:21.564
EPISODE 16
LET'S GO HUNTING!

02:27.696 --> 02:29.823
Wow, super kewl!

02:30.323 --> 02:34.577
Keeping a nimble rat
within range won't be easy,

02:34.911 --> 02:38.497
but shooting these bearings
will expand it to about 20 meters.

02:39.040 --> 02:41.917
And of course,
they're useless against Stands.

02:42.210 --> 02:44.921
Use them for downing the user.

02:45.588 --> 02:46.255
Give it a try.

02:46.339 --> 02:48.007
I have to use 'em, too?

02:48.758 --> 02:50.050
I don't know…

02:50.719 --> 02:54.305
I don't have the concentration
for ball sports and stuff.

03:07.944 --> 03:09.570
I almost got the second one!

03:09.696 --> 03:12.365
Not bad. I'd give you an 85.

03:13.074 --> 03:15.951
Before we begin our hunt,
you have to remember one thing:

03:16.244 --> 03:18.079
When dealing with live animals,

03:18.163 --> 03:20.957
you have to place
composure over speed.

03:22.542 --> 03:24.627
If you find the rat
within range and miss,

03:24.919 --> 03:27.963
don't expect it
to come within range again.

03:28.590 --> 03:31.050
So hold your fire until you're
positive you can hit your target.

03:31.634 --> 03:33.761
No pressure though.

03:34.262 --> 03:35.304
Got it?

03:35.680 --> 03:39.141
He sure knows how
to make a guy feel at ease.

03:41.227 --> 03:43.520
Seems Akira Otoishi shot the rat

03:43.646 --> 03:45.773
near this irrigation canal.

03:46.524 --> 03:49.193
Given the location, it was probably
the common Brown Rat.

03:49.778 --> 03:51.279
Brown Rats are agile swimmers,

03:51.362 --> 03:54.114
highly adaptable,
and can eat practically anything.

03:55.074 --> 03:58.494
Larger rats can grow up to
20 - 30 centimeters long.

03:58.870 --> 04:00.997
And some can weigh
as much as one kilogram.

04:01.539 --> 04:03.082
Their horizontal leap
is about 2 meters.

04:04.250 --> 04:05.209
Found it.

04:05.293 --> 04:07.670
Aren't those bird tracks?

04:07.879 --> 04:10.756
Its forefeet have four digits,
its hindfeet have five.

04:11.299 --> 04:13.426
It's making this S-shape
because it's dragging something.

04:14.010 --> 04:15.553
These markings are tail tracks.

04:16.221 --> 04:18.348
The rat must be
about 20 centimeters long.

04:18.556 --> 04:21.016
I can't tell how many,
but we've definitely got a rat.

04:22.227 --> 04:23.645
There's a tick on this leaf.

04:23.770 --> 04:26.230
This is a stomping ground for rats.

04:28.233 --> 04:31.778
There's no question,
somewhere in that drain is a nest.

04:33.571 --> 04:37.866
For now, we'll set a trap and
see what the video camera picks up.

04:38.993 --> 04:40.160
That's one of those cameras

04:40.245 --> 04:42.205
that lets you watch
while you're recording, right?

04:44.457 --> 04:46.542
You're not gonna use cheese?

04:47.460 --> 04:49.086
It's a hunk of tempura.

04:49.671 --> 04:51.964
Cheese is too luxurious for a rat.

04:57.387 --> 05:00.014
What's with all these flies…

05:00.974 --> 05:01.808
Jotaro!

05:02.308 --> 05:03.559
Th-These are…

05:10.316 --> 05:11.817
Dead rats?

05:11.943 --> 05:13.903
Yeah, no shit!

05:13.987 --> 05:16.531
It looks like a block
of jellied fish.

05:19.826 --> 05:22.161
Why are you poking it?!

05:22.245 --> 05:23.246
It's flesh.

05:24.205 --> 05:25.206
At some point,

05:25.290 --> 05:27.750
the flesh of these rats
melted and later congealed.

05:28.459 --> 05:31.378
Something melted their flesh
subcutaneously, killing them.

05:31.713 --> 05:35.258
How does that even happen?

05:35.466 --> 05:36.592
I don't have the answer…

05:36.885 --> 05:40.722
Safe to say it's the doing
of that rat we're after.

05:41.055 --> 05:42.264
You think it used a Stand to…

05:42.974 --> 05:47.103
It exterminated its fellow rats
to dominate the territory.

05:47.228 --> 05:48.103
Which means…

05:48.771 --> 05:51.857
It's highly likely the rat's making
a nest in that drain.

05:52.859 --> 05:54.235
The question is,

05:54.360 --> 05:57.363
has whatever's done this
done anything else?

06:04.245 --> 06:07.456
Looks like the drainage canal
continues on to that house.

06:08.207 --> 06:10.083
We might already be too late.

06:10.376 --> 06:11.752
R-Really?

06:12.045 --> 06:15.631
I see a chicken coop,
but no chickens.

06:16.883 --> 06:19.302
And no sign of activity
in that house, either.

06:20.094 --> 06:21.512
Their cars are still parked
in the garage,

06:21.596 --> 06:23.556
and the front door isn't locked.

06:24.849 --> 06:26.100
The rat must be there.

06:26.225 --> 06:27.559
It doesn't look good.

06:27.685 --> 06:30.688
The inhabitants of this house
have likely already been killed.

06:31.397 --> 06:33.690
Come on, we have to investigate.

06:43.117 --> 06:45.869
The rat will let us
approach up to a point.

06:46.371 --> 06:50.249
It knows most humans
are too slow to ever catch it.

06:50.959 --> 06:53.753
It's not expecting us
to use it as target practice.

06:53.878 --> 06:57.548
That's how we'll close in
and put it down with one shot.

06:59.133 --> 06:59.883
Bingo.

07:01.135 --> 07:02.219
Rat droppings.

07:04.305 --> 07:06.557
No grass or grain here.

07:06.808 --> 07:07.558
It's meat.

07:08.393 --> 07:10.019
The droppings continue
into this room.

07:10.311 --> 07:11.061
Let's look.

07:11.312 --> 07:12.062
Right.

07:22.323 --> 07:23.198
What is that?

07:23.449 --> 07:26.118
A refrigerator compressor?

07:28.830 --> 07:30.206
<i>What the heck?</i>

07:30.623 --> 07:33.626
<i>Did this refrigerator
open its own door?</i>

07:34.127 --> 07:36.462
<i>Did the door's magnet give out?</i>

07:37.422 --> 07:39.048
<i>Shit! There it is!</i>

07:39.132 --> 07:41.300
<i>Holy shit! It's right there!</i>

07:41.384 --> 07:43.844
<i>So that's what opened the door!</i>

07:43.928 --> 07:47.056
<i>Rats can open refrigerator doors?!</i>

07:47.348 --> 07:50.517
<i>No way… Someone must've
forgotten to shut the door.</i>

07:50.852 --> 07:54.689
<i>Come on, are you really
that gullible, Josuke?</i>

07:55.064 --> 07:57.399
<i>This rat's a Stand user!</i>

07:57.859 --> 07:58.693
Jo—

07:59.819 --> 08:01.237
<i>Jotaro's gone!</i>

08:01.863 --> 08:03.614
<i>He went into the next room.</i>

08:07.785 --> 08:11.121
<i>Great. Our eyes've met.</i>

08:14.208 --> 08:15.584
<i>Th-This is…</i>

08:16.878 --> 08:18.671
<i>The rat did this?!</i>

08:20.548 --> 08:21.757
<i>They're still alive…</i>

08:23.384 --> 08:26.887
<i>Did that rat disfigure the people
of this house with its Stand</i>

08:26.971 --> 08:29.431
<i>to then store them in the fridge?</i>

08:30.224 --> 08:32.267
<i>And it's eating them!</i>

08:32.351 --> 08:34.978
<i>Damn it…
Jotaro's not coming back.</i>

08:35.063 --> 08:37.398
<i>I'm gonna have to kill this thing.</i>

08:38.066 --> 08:39.484
<i>When dealing with live animals,</i>

08:39.567 --> 08:42.319
<i>it's composure above speed.</i>

08:43.196 --> 08:45.948
<i>If I don't knock him off on
my first try, he'll know my range.</i>

08:46.574 --> 08:48.617
<i>That's what he said Shit…</i>

08:48.868 --> 08:50.286
<i>He sure can lay on the pressure!</i>

08:51.162 --> 08:52.413
<i>Of course,</i>

08:52.497 --> 08:55.124
<i>the table and chair are positioned
just enough to be in my way</i>

08:55.708 --> 08:57.918
<i>I gotta make sure I sink
this ball bearing</i>

08:58.002 --> 08:59.294
<i>right between his eyes.</i>

08:59.754 --> 09:01.797
<i>Now stay right there…</i>

09:03.508 --> 09:05.885
<i>Crap! He stopped eating.</i>

09:06.135 --> 09:08.053
<i>If I move any more,
he'll run for it!</i>

09:08.971 --> 09:10.514
<i>Fudge it! It'll be an adventure.</i>

09:10.723 --> 09:12.683
<i>I'll blast him from right here!</i>

09:13.935 --> 09:15.227
<i>He's moving! Now!</i>

09:17.563 --> 09:18.313
CRUSH

09:18.689 --> 09:19.481
Yes!

09:21.776 --> 09:23.235
It didn't kill him!

09:26.030 --> 09:27.156
He's come out!

09:27.281 --> 09:29.157
That must be his Stand!

09:29.283 --> 09:31.159
You wanna take me on, huh?

09:31.285 --> 09:33.203
I'd watch out if I were you!

09:34.330 --> 09:37.291
My next shot will
knock you out for good!

09:38.042 --> 09:40.544
<i>Dammit!
He's running under the table!</i>

09:41.379 --> 09:42.546
<i>No, you don't!</i>

09:45.091 --> 09:46.926
Jotaro, what the hell
are you doing over there?!

09:47.009 --> 09:48.301
The rat's here!

09:54.767 --> 09:56.018
<i>That shape…</i>

09:57.103 --> 09:59.188
Uh-oh! Its Stand shoots!

10:03.234 --> 10:05.527
<i>Now what? Slap it away
with my bare hands?</i>

10:05.695 --> 10:07.697
<i>On second thought,
that's kinda gross…</i>

10:09.448 --> 10:10.532
<i>Which is it?</i>

10:10.616 --> 10:13.368
<i>Did I hit it, or did I miss?</i>

10:15.955 --> 10:17.247
Little bastard!

10:21.127 --> 10:23.379
Yeah! I got him!

10:23.838 --> 10:27.049
It wasn't his forehead,
but he's a goner.

10:27.175 --> 10:28.509
That was close…

10:29.677 --> 10:32.304
Jotaro, over here!

10:32.388 --> 10:35.474
I got the rat! It's over!

10:37.393 --> 10:39.478
Jeez. What were you doing?

10:39.562 --> 10:41.772
You went missing right
when I needed ya.

10:41.856 --> 10:44.066
I got lonely back there.

10:44.192 --> 10:46.027
Well, it's the funniest thing…

10:46.235 --> 10:48.403
Lucky for me,
that shot didn't go balls up.

10:48.613 --> 10:51.073
For me, at least.

10:52.408 --> 10:55.327
His Stand shot
some needle-like things at me.

10:55.995 --> 10:59.415
I bet those are what
turn your flesh to goo.

11:00.208 --> 11:03.252
He got the people in this house,
but they're still alive.

11:03.502 --> 11:05.670
I'll fix 'em right up
with Shining Diamond.

11:07.048 --> 11:09.425
If we don't hunt him down
by sundown,

11:09.550 --> 11:10.884
things might get even messier.

11:11.219 --> 11:11.969
Huh?

11:12.678 --> 11:15.722
That wasn't the only rat.
Another one got me.

11:16.891 --> 11:18.893
Jotaro! Y-Your hand…

11:19.060 --> 11:20.811
It happened in the room over there.

11:20.895 --> 11:22.813
I could have dodged it…

11:22.897 --> 11:26.400
Catching its needle for analysis
wasn't the best choice.

11:27.151 --> 11:28.485
All it takes is a touch,

11:28.653 --> 11:32.823
and its Stand's poison begins
to permeate, melting even Stands.

11:34.200 --> 11:35.618
Five or six hits,

11:35.701 --> 11:37.744
and you'll turn into
a quivering mass of flesh.

11:40.081 --> 11:42.041
<i>Thank god that thing didn't hit me!</i>

11:42.208 --> 11:44.710
<i>Who knew my personality
would come in handy.</i>

11:46.003 --> 11:48.422
The rat ran outside
after he hit me.

11:48.547 --> 11:51.967
It must've figured out you killed
its relative in the kitchen.

11:53.302 --> 11:54.094
Sorry to bother,

11:54.178 --> 11:56.847
but I'm sort of counting on
your curative powers here.

11:56.931 --> 11:58.682
O-Oh, right!

11:59.600 --> 12:00.851
<i>Damn it!</i>

12:00.935 --> 12:03.479
<i>Why'd those little S.O.B.s
have to multiply?</i>

12:08.776 --> 12:11.487
STAR PLATINUM

12:12.780 --> 12:15.365
<i>Hello, this is the Speedwagon
Foundation research department.</i>

12:15.783 --> 12:18.327
Hello, this is Jotaro Kujo.

12:18.536 --> 12:19.870
<i>Jotaro!</i>

12:19.954 --> 12:22.373
<i>We've tried to reach you
several times.</i>

12:22.623 --> 12:24.916
I was hunting and
turned the ringer off.

12:25.001 --> 12:27.128
This isn't about Otoishi, is it?

12:27.295 --> 12:31.795
<i>Yes. Akira Otoishi was covering up
his shooting of two rats.</i>

12:32.425 --> 12:33.551
Got it.

12:33.634 --> 12:35.969
Two, not three or four, right?

12:36.178 --> 12:37.971
<i>Yes, we're certain of it.</i>

12:39.557 --> 12:41.642
Good grief, Akira Otoishi…

12:43.811 --> 12:45.312
Way to go.

12:46.105 --> 12:47.564
When it comes to its own territory,

12:47.648 --> 12:50.525
it will kill everything,
humans and rats alike.

12:50.818 --> 12:52.820
It cares only about itself.

12:53.195 --> 12:57.695
It's time its life on earth
comes to an end.

12:58.659 --> 13:00.869
Jotaro, wait!

13:00.995 --> 13:04.039
A teeny-weeny rat just
ran into an open field…

13:04.165 --> 13:06.250
How exactly do you plan
on tracking this thing down?

13:06.667 --> 13:09.795
Ernest Thompson Seton famously said

13:10.004 --> 13:12.631
there is no animal
that cannot be tracked.

13:13.049 --> 13:17.219
Rats are known to
avoid unfamiliar paths.

13:17.303 --> 13:19.805
Which means, its route of escape

13:19.889 --> 13:21.682
had to be that irrigation channel.

13:23.351 --> 13:24.894
And there's something else
about rats…

13:25.853 --> 13:27.396
Without the constant
intake of food,

13:27.772 --> 13:29.690
within hours,
they'll starve to death.

13:31.734 --> 13:34.528
There…
Those are fresh bite marks.

13:34.653 --> 13:37.072
Yes! This is awesome!

13:37.198 --> 13:39.533
We'll corner
that little buck-toothed bastard!

13:41.869 --> 13:43.412
Take a look at this.

13:43.579 --> 13:47.291
I don't think it even
looked at our bait.

13:47.500 --> 13:48.542
We got him on tape.

13:56.175 --> 13:59.136
Its ear looks like
a bug-eaten leaf.

13:59.220 --> 14:01.931
This little guy is "Bug-Eaten."

14:02.306 --> 14:03.557
Look how careful he's being…

14:04.266 --> 14:05.767
Unlike earlier, Bug-Eaten

14:06.102 --> 14:10.189
is going to be extra careful to
not let us within 20 meters of him.

14:12.400 --> 14:13.818
These are live rifle rounds.

14:14.235 --> 14:17.404
Worst case, we've got these to use.

14:17.571 --> 14:19.030
L-Live rounds?!

14:19.573 --> 14:22.826
Due to drag, ball bearings lose
a great deal of accuracy

14:22.910 --> 14:25.662
when traveling over 20 meters.

14:26.414 --> 14:30.876
With a bullet nose like this,
we'll be okay up to 70 meters.

14:31.085 --> 14:33.796
Am I going to have to launch that
with my Stand's hand, too?

14:34.255 --> 14:36.340
I don't think I'm ready for that.

14:37.842 --> 14:40.636
Apparently not.
Then it'll have to be me.

14:44.223 --> 14:46.058
Hold it right there…

14:46.267 --> 14:48.143
What do you mean by that?

14:48.227 --> 14:49.978
That really pissed me off.

14:52.148 --> 14:55.067
Remember, I'm the one
who nailed that other one!

14:55.151 --> 14:57.820
Sure, it wasn't exactly perfect,
but…

14:57.945 --> 14:59.947
Guess you're right.
You get two then.

15:00.030 --> 15:01.239
Huh?

15:05.077 --> 15:08.413
<i>More pressure…</i>

15:40.362 --> 15:43.073
Careful. This puddle's got leeches.

15:43.157 --> 15:44.032
What?!

15:51.999 --> 15:52.749
Shit…

15:53.125 --> 15:53.917
What now?

15:54.585 --> 15:56.420
Careful, Josuke.

15:56.837 --> 15:59.089
The footprints suddenly stop here.

16:00.049 --> 16:01.383
What is this?!

16:01.509 --> 16:03.761
Why would they suddenly stop?

16:04.220 --> 16:06.055
I know! It must be underground.

16:06.180 --> 16:08.015
It must've burrowed
a hole and covered itself.

16:08.307 --> 16:09.057
No!

16:09.683 --> 16:11.351
It's called backtracking…

16:11.936 --> 16:14.146
I didn't expect rats
to be capable of this, too.

16:14.313 --> 16:15.731
Backtracking?

16:16.232 --> 16:20.236
<i>Backtracking is the way in which
a wild animal will reverse itself</i>

16:20.319 --> 16:24.031
<i>by stepping in its own tracks
to hide from predators.</i>

16:24.365 --> 16:26.075
<i>In Japan, the behavior
has been observed</i>

16:26.158 --> 16:28.577
<i>with brown bears,
weasels, and rabbits.</i>

16:28.953 --> 16:32.164
<i>But never with any species of rat.</i>

16:33.832 --> 16:35.792
So basically, what that means is…

16:36.210 --> 16:39.129
the rat pulled a fast one on us.

16:39.588 --> 16:41.881
Looks like things've
taken a turn for the worse.

16:42.049 --> 16:42.966
With this kind of terrain…

16:43.092 --> 16:45.594
we may've just gone
from hunters to prey.

16:48.472 --> 16:51.016
I have this creepy feeling
we're being watched.

16:51.684 --> 16:53.644
I think we better hide
behind a rock.

16:53.727 --> 16:54.978
No sudden movements…

16:57.273 --> 17:00.651
Bug-Eaten's attack
isn't too fast for us to see.

17:01.151 --> 17:02.944
Keep an eye out
for the point of fire.

17:03.112 --> 17:06.782
If we can find where it's hiding,
we'll snipe it instead.

17:14.873 --> 17:15.957
What the hell?!

17:20.921 --> 17:21.671
Wha—?!

17:22.172 --> 17:25.425
<i>That dirty rodent used
the rat trap on us?</i>

17:26.760 --> 17:29.262
Star Platinum, The World!

17:30.723 --> 17:31.974
Good grief.

17:39.607 --> 17:40.357
Don't worry.

17:40.649 --> 17:42.651
I removed the needle
before the poison spread,

17:43.068 --> 17:45.236
along with the affected tissue.

17:45.404 --> 17:46.655
Put a bandage on it.

17:48.490 --> 17:51.034
I also located
his general whereabouts.

17:51.619 --> 17:54.872
Halfway up the hill,
near those three rocks.

17:57.207 --> 18:01.085
Amazing! You and that rat!

18:01.211 --> 18:04.881
Guess the only chump now is me…

18:10.471 --> 18:12.181
It's 60 meters away.

18:12.681 --> 18:15.308
I see no sign of another
needle launch.

18:15.392 --> 18:18.144
It knows random fire will
give away its precise location,

18:18.228 --> 18:20.188
and open itself up to attack.

18:20.981 --> 18:22.357
Stubborn bastard.

18:22.775 --> 18:24.610
Why are you praising that damn rat?

18:25.152 --> 18:27.737
We need to act.

18:28.489 --> 18:30.199
Well said, Josuke.

18:30.658 --> 18:33.619
We need to give this
everything we've got,

18:33.827 --> 18:35.829
or Bug-Eaten's gonna
take us both out.

18:35.996 --> 18:38.373
I'll give you all four rounds.

18:41.085 --> 18:44.296
At this distance,
it'll rise like a slider,

18:44.672 --> 18:46.590
so aim one centimeter
below the target.

18:49.176 --> 18:51.386
Jotaro? What are you going to do?

18:51.720 --> 18:54.013
I'm moving in
so he'll shoot his needles.

18:54.848 --> 18:57.976
You, Josuke, are going to
determine his location…

18:58.852 --> 19:00.854
Then you're going to shoot him.

19:00.938 --> 19:03.398
W-What?!

19:04.191 --> 19:06.318
You don't have a choice.

19:09.697 --> 19:12.449
Even if one or two
of his needles get me,

19:12.533 --> 19:15.160
Shining Diamond can heal me.

19:16.412 --> 19:20.207
Remember, Josuke,
you can't heal yourself.

19:26.839 --> 19:29.258
It's balls to the wall, Josuke!

19:32.553 --> 19:34.346
Could I have a second
to mentally prepare?

19:35.431 --> 19:37.641
Star Platinum, The World!

19:48.569 --> 19:49.528
Find him?

19:49.653 --> 19:53.281
N-No…
As soon as he fired, he moved!

19:53.490 --> 19:56.034
I'll try to get closer while
going up the side of the hill.

19:57.077 --> 19:58.745
Watch for the moment he fires.

19:58.829 --> 20:00.372
The moment he fires…

20:00.456 --> 20:02.666
<i>Damn this pressure!</i>

20:07.880 --> 20:09.298
There! I see him!

20:14.636 --> 20:15.803
What?!

20:15.888 --> 20:18.265
That bastard predicted I'd dodge,

20:18.348 --> 20:20.767
then fired the needles
at the rocks?

20:20.851 --> 20:22.143
They ricocheted?

20:28.650 --> 20:29.609
Jotaro!

20:29.735 --> 20:32.279
Quit staring at me, Josuke!

20:32.362 --> 20:34.072
Keep your eye on the rat!

20:34.156 --> 20:36.575
The moment he attacks,
obliterate him!

20:36.658 --> 20:37.825
<i>This isn't good</i>

20:38.035 --> 20:40.704
<i>I've got four rounds,
but no more chances.</i>

20:40.788 --> 20:42.581
<i>If I waste any time…</i>

20:42.664 --> 20:44.499
Here we go, Josuke.

20:49.797 --> 20:52.216
<i>There! Same spot as before.</i>

20:52.299 --> 20:55.302
<i>But he's hiding behind the rocks.</i>

20:55.385 --> 20:58.179
<i>Shit! If only he was
looking over here…</i>

21:02.810 --> 21:04.228
<i>I've gotta do this!</i>

21:04.770 --> 21:07.355
<i>I'll just have to hit
a tiny target!</i>

21:09.775 --> 21:12.110
I suddenly feel
that fighting spirit.

21:12.194 --> 21:14.654
I'm gonna get you, little fucker.

21:24.581 --> 21:27.542
Josuke missed…

21:37.219 --> 21:38.428
So you did look.

21:39.054 --> 21:41.431
I thought my miss
would make you look

21:41.515 --> 21:43.058
and turn your body toward me.

21:44.643 --> 21:47.687
Soon I'll have you
right in my crosshairs.

22:01.451 --> 22:04.203
So I guess I wasn't a chump,
after all.

22:04.538 --> 22:09.038
Call me Josuke Higashikata,
vanquisher of pressure and stress!

22:09.251 --> 22:12.045
Akira Otoishi's
mutant Stand rats…

22:12.129 --> 22:14.756
calls to mind our own destruction
of the environment…

22:14.882 --> 22:16.091
Not exactly sure
how I should feel…

22:17.301 --> 22:19.469
At least Josuke's a dependable guy.

22:20.512 --> 22:21.596
Good grief.

22:21.972 --> 22:24.182
Maybe this means
a little peace of mind.

23:38.757 --> 23:41.926
EPISODE 17
ROHAN KISHIBE'S ADVENTURE
